# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Paano kalkulahin ang mga custom na bound para sa pinakabagong bersyon ng Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds"
msgstr "Paano kalkulahin ang mga custom na bound"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/custom-bounds.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`compute_forward_bounds` and `compute_backward_bounds` are convenience wrappers. Both are built from\n"
"the same three pieces, which the public API exposes:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `compute_forward_bounds` at `compute_backward_bounds` ay mga convenience wrapper. Pareho silang binuo mula sa\n"
"parehong tatlong piyesa, na inilalantad ng public API:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **norm function**, which bounds a single evolved Pauli error term\n"
msgstr "Isang **norm function**, na nagbo-bound sa isang na-evolve na Pauli error term\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **light cone**, which seeds what the error terms are evolved toward\n"
msgstr "Isang **light cone**, na nagtatakda kung saan ine-evolve ang mga error term\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_bounds`, which iterates the circuit and distributes the per-term work\n"
msgstr "`compute_bounds`, na nag-iterate sa circuit at nagpapamahagi ng trabaho kada term\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assembling them yourself means you can bound something the wrappers don't cover. This guide works\n"
"through one case where that is worth doing: a **mirror circuit**, where the usual backward bound is\n"
"needlessly loose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-assemble sa mga ito nang mag-isa ay nangangahulugang makakapag-bound ka ng bagay na hindi sakop ng mga wrapper. Tinatalakay ng gabay na ito\n"
"ang isang kasong sulit gawin ito: isang **mirror circuit**, kung saan ang karaniwang backward bound ay\n"
"walang saysay na maluwag.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the wrappers actually do {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"
msgstr "Ang aktwal na ginagawa ng mga wrapper {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two wrappers differ in the three places listed above:\n"
msgstr "Magkaiba ang dalawang wrapper sa tatlong lugar na nakalista sa itaas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| circuit | as given | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| norm function | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, against the observable | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, against the initial state |\n"
"| light cone | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, seeded from the observable | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, seeded from every active qubit |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| circuit | gaya ng ibinigay | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| norm function | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, laban sa observable | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, laban sa initial state |\n"
"| light cone | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, mula sa observable | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, mula sa bawat aktibong qubit |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The forward bound asks *\"How much can this error change the observable I am about to measure?\"* and\n"
"answers it with the spectral norm of a commutator. The backward bound asks *\"How much can this error\n"
"change the state I started from?\"* and answers with a nuclear norm, taking that state to be the\n"
"all-zero state on every active qubit. They are different questions, and each is the right one for\n"
"errors in its own half of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinatanong ng forward bound ang *\"Gaano mababago ng error na ito ang observable na susukatin ko?\"* at\n"
"sinasagot ito gamit ang spectral norm ng isang commutator. Tinatanong ng backward bound ang *\"Gaano mababago ng error na ito\n"
"ang state na pinagmulan ko?\"* at sinasagot gamit ang nuclear norm, na ang state ay ang\n"
"all-zero state sa bawat aktibong qubit. Magkaibang tanong sila, at bawat isa ang tama para sa\n"
"mga error sa sarili nitong kalahati ng circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mirror circuit case {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"
msgstr "Ang kaso ng mirror circuit {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mirror circuit applies some unitary and then undoes it: $U^\\dagger U$. These appear whenever\n"
"the ideal outcome has to be known exactly (generally Loschmidt echoes, randomized benchmarking, and\n"
"verification experiments).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mirror circuit ay naglalapat ng isang unitary at pagkatapos ay binabawi ito: $U^\\dagger U$. Lumilitaw ang mga ito tuwing\n"
"kailangang tiyak na alam ang ideal na resulta (karaniwan sa mga Loschmidt echo, randomized benchmarking, at\n"
"mga eksperimento sa verification).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mirror circuits have a property the generic backward bound cannot exploit. Because the second half\n"
"is the inverse of the first, *evolving an error backward to the initial state* traverses the same\n"
"gates as *evolving it forward to the observable*. The two questions coincide, so the sharper\n"
"forward-style bound is valid for the backward direction too.\n"
msgstr ""
"May katangian ang mga mirror circuit na hindi magagamit ng generic na backward bound. Dahil ang ikalawang kalahati\n"
"ay ang inverse ng una, ang *pag-evolve ng error pabalik sa initial state* ay dumadaan sa parehong\n"
"mga gate gaya ng *pag-evolve nito pasulong sa observable*. Nagtutugma ang dalawang tanong, kaya ang mas matalas na\n"
"forward-style na bound ay valid din para sa backward na direksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the custom bound {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"
msgstr "I-assemble ang custom na bound {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recipe keeps what `compute_backward_bounds` does with the circuit (strip the measurements,\n"
"invert it, and iterate it with `backwards=True`) and substitutes the other two pieces: the forward\n"
"norm function, and a light cone seeded from the observable with `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"exactly as `compute_forward_bounds` seeds its own. Each substitution is one line.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinananatili ng recipe ang ginagawa ng `compute_backward_bounds` sa circuit (alisin ang mga measurement,\n"
"i-invert ito, at i-iterate ito gamit ang `backwards=True`) at pinapalitan ang dalawa pang piyesa: ang forward\n"
"norm function, at isang light cone na mula sa observable gamit ang `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"eksakto kung paano binubuo ng `compute_forward_bounds` ang sarili nito. Isang linya ang bawat pagpapalit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much it gains {#how-much-it-gains}"
msgstr "Gaano ito kalaki ang naidaragdag {#how-much-it-gains}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Comparing against the stock backward bound on the same circuit, summarized the same way as in the\n"
"[configuration guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): the mean bound and its standard deviation,\n"
"followed by the share of terms bounded by 0, with a bound computed in between, and left at the\n"
"trivial 2.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Paghahambing sa stock na backward bound sa parehong circuit, na binuod sa parehong paraan tulad sa\n"
"[configuration guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): ang mean na bound at ang standard deviation nito,\n"
"kasunod ang bahagi ng mga term na may bound na 0, may nakalkulang bound sa pagitan, at nanatili sa\n"
"trivial na 2.0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The stock backward bound sits near the trivial value of 2.0, which carries almost no information. On\n"
"a mirror circuit, every error is \"close to the initial state\" in the sense that bound measures, so\n"
"it cannot discriminate between terms. The custom bound is several times tighter and bounds many of the terms by 0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang stock na backward bound ay malapit sa trivial na halaga na 2.0, na halos walang dalang impormasyon. Sa\n"
"isang mirror circuit, bawat error ay \"malapit sa initial state\" sa kahulugang sinusukat ng bound na iyon, kaya\n"
"hindi nito mapag-iiba ang mga term. Ang custom na bound ay ilang beses na mas mahigpit at nagbo-bound sa maraming term sa 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To check the implementation, the two can be compared box by box. For every box, the\n"
"custom backward bound comes out **identical** to that same box's forward bound, up to rounding\n"
"error. Both bound the same error at the same point in the circuit, and on a mirror circuit the gates\n"
"after that point cancel to the inverse of the gates before it, so the two computations evaluate the\n"
"same quantity from opposite ends:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para suriin ang implementasyon, maaaring ihambing ang dalawa kada box. Para sa bawat box, ang\n"
"custom na backward bound ay lumalabas na **magkapareho** sa forward bound ng parehong box, hanggang sa rounding\n"
"error. Parehong nagbo-bound ang dalawa sa parehong error sa parehong punto sa circuit, at sa mirror circuit, ang mga gate\n"
"pagkatapos ng puntong iyon ay nagka-cancel bilang inverse ng mga gate bago nito, kaya ang dalawang pagkalkula ay sumusuri sa\n"
"parehong dami mula sa magkabilang dulo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** This equality is a property of the mirror structure, not of the technique. On a circuit\n"
"that is not self-inverting, the same substitution still runs but no longer computes a *valid* bound\n"
"for the backward direction: it answers the forward question about a circuit half where that\n"
"question does not apply. **Only use this when the second half of your circuit inverts the\n"
"first.**\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandaan:** Ang pagkakapantay na ito ay katangian ng istruktura ng mirror, hindi ng teknik. Sa circuit na\n"
"hindi self-inverting, tumatakbo pa rin ang parehong pagpapalit pero hindi na nito kinakalkula ang *valid* na bound\n"
"para sa backward na direksyon: sinasagot nito ang forward na tanong tungkol sa kalahati ng circuit kung saan hindi\n"
"nalalapat ang tanong. **Gamitin lang ito kapag ang ikalawang kalahati ng circuit mo ay nag-i-invert sa\n"
"una.**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</div>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed it into the rest of the workflow {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Ipasok ito sa natitirang bahagi ng workflow {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is an ordinary `Bounds` dictionary, so everything that follows is unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Ang resulta ay karaniwang `Bounds` dictionary, kaya walang nagbabago sa lahat ng susunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a mirror circuit there is also no reason to compute either bound for the whole circuit. The\n"
"forward bounds are only needed for the boxes of $U^\\dagger$, counted from the end, and the backward\n"
"bounds only for the boxes of $U$, counted from the start. `max_num_boxes` therefore limits each of\n"
"them to half of the noisy boxes, and `merge_bounds` joins the two halves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mirror circuit, wala ring dahilan para kalkulahin ang alinmang bound para sa buong circuit. Ang\n"
"forward na mga bound ay kailangan lang para sa mga box ng $U^\\dagger$, na binibilang mula sa dulo, at ang backward\n"
"na mga bound ay para lang sa mga box ng $U$, na binibilang mula sa simula. Kaya nililimitahan ng `max_num_boxes` ang bawat isa\n"
"sa kalahati ng mga maingay na box, at pinagsasama ng `merge_bounds` ang dalawang kalahati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is how the bounds are used in practice, and it means the box-for-box comparison above is no\n"
"longer available: it needs both bounds for every box. It is a check of the implementation for this guide, not workflow step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ganito ginagamit ang mga bound sa praktika, at nangangahulugan itong hindi na magagamit ang paghahambing na box-por-box sa itaas:\n"
"kailangan nito ang parehong bound para sa bawat box. Isa itong pagsusuri ng implementasyon para sa gabay na ito, hindi hakbang ng workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the stock backward bounds, the sampling overhead is far larger. `merge_bounds` uses the\n"
"backward bounds up to one switch point in the circuit and the forward bounds from there on,\n"
"choosing the point that minimizes the total bias. With each bound computed for one half, that point\n"
"falls in the middle of the circuit, so the boxes of $U$ are covered by backward bounds alone. The\n"
"stock backward bound is close to the trivial 2.0 there, which drives the overhead up. The custom\n"
"one is as tight as the forward bound would have been, so the overhead matches that of the complete\n"
"forward bounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga stock na backward bound, mas malaki nang malayo ang sampling overhead. Ginagamit ng `merge_bounds` ang\n"
"backward na mga bound hanggang sa isang switch point sa circuit at ang forward na mga bound mula roon,\n"
"pinipili ang puntong nagpapaliit sa kabuuang bias. Kapag ang bawat bound ay kinalkula para sa isang kalahati, ang puntong iyon\n"
"ay babagsak sa gitna ng circuit, kaya ang mga box ng $U$ ay sakop ng backward na mga bound lang. Ang\n"
"stock na backward bound ay malapit sa trivial na 2.0 doon, na nagpapataas ng overhead. Ang custom\n"
"ay kasinghigpit ng magiging forward bound, kaya ang overhead ay tumutugma sa kumpletong\n"
"forward na mga bound.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That raises the obvious question of why to bother, when the complete forward bounds alone give the\n"
"same result. The answer is cost. A forward bound for a box early in the circuit evolves its error\n"
"through the rest of $U$ and then all of $U^\\dagger$, which is the longest and widest evolution in\n"
"the circuit. The evolved operator can grow exponentially in the number of non-Clifford gates\n"
"it passes through, and computing the commutator's spectral norm gets exponentially more expensive as\n"
"the light cone widens. In the half-and-half approach, no error is evolved through more than half of\n"
"the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil dito, lumilitaw ang malinaw na tanong kung bakit pa mag-aabala, kung ang kumpletong forward na mga bound lang ay nagbibigay ng\n"
"parehong resulta. Ang sagot ay gastos. Ang forward bound para sa box sa unang bahagi ng circuit ay ine-evolve ang error nito\n"
"sa natitirang bahagi ng $U$ at pagkatapos ay sa buong $U^\\dagger$, na siyang pinakamahaba at pinakamalapad na evolution sa\n"
"circuit. Maaaring lumaki nang exponential ang na-evolve na operator ayon sa bilang ng mga non-Clifford gate\n"
"na dinadaanan nito, at ang pagkalkula ng spectral norm ng commutator ay nagiging exponentially na mas magastos habang\n"
"lumalapad ang light cone. Sa half-and-half na paraan, walang error na ine-evolve sa higit sa kalahati ng\n"
"circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The saving therefore grows with the circuit depth. More importantly, the complete forward\n"
"bounds stop being computable long before the halfway ones do. Once the evolutions of the early\n"
"boxes exceed `evolution_max_terms` or `eigval_max_qubits`, their bounds are truncated or fall back\n"
"to the triangle inequality, and eventually they cost too much to compute. Wherever that point\n"
"lies, the half-and-half approach only needs it to fall somewhere in the first half of the circuit.\n"
"The forward bounds have to reach no further than the middle, and on a mirror circuit, the backward\n"
"bounds for the boxes of $U$ evolve their errors back to the start through as much of the\n"
"circuit as the forward bounds for the matching boxes of $U^\\dagger$ do to the end, so they run out\n"
"at the same depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya lumalaki ang natitipid kasabay ng lalim ng circuit. Mas mahalaga, ang kumpletong forward\n"
"na mga bound ay hindi na makakalkula nang mas maaga kaysa sa mga halfway. Kapag ang mga evolution ng mga maagang\n"
"box ay lumampas sa `evolution_max_terms` o `eigval_max_qubits`, ang mga bound nila ay pinuputol o bumabalik\n"
"sa triangle inequality, at sa huli ay masyado nang magastos kalkulahin. Saanman ang puntong iyon,\n"
"ang half-and-half na paraan ay nangangailangan lang na mahulog ito sa isang lugar sa unang kalahati ng circuit.\n"
"Ang mga forward na bound ay hindi kailangang lumampas sa gitna, at sa mirror circuit, ang backward\n"
"na mga bound para sa mga box ng $U$ ay ine-evolve ang mga error nila pabalik sa simula sa kasing-daming bahagi ng\n"
"circuit gaya ng ginagawa ng mga forward na bound para sa katugmang mga box ng $U^\\dagger$ patungo sa dulo, kaya sila ay nauubusan\n"
"sa parehong lalim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** Why compute backward bounds for the boxes of $U$, when the forward bounds of the\n"
"boxes of $U^\\dagger$ look like they should hold the same numbers? Because the boxes are not mirror\n"
"images of each other. Each box injects its noise on one side of its gates, and the inverse layers of\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ are separate boxes with noise models of their own, so the box that mirrors a box of $U$\n"
"sees its errors at a different point in the circuit. Therefore, their bounds only partly agree, and\n"
"the bounds for the boxes of $U$ have to be computed for those boxes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tandaan:** Bakit kakalkulahin ang backward na mga bound para sa mga box ng $U$, kung ang forward na mga bound ng\n"
"mga box ng $U^\\dagger$ ay mukhang dapat may parehong mga numero? Dahil ang mga box ay hindi mirror\n"
"image ng isa't isa. Bawat box ay nag-i-inject ng noise nito sa isang panig ng mga gate nito, at ang mga inverse layer ng\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ ay hiwalay na mga box na may sarili nilang noise model, kaya ang box na kamukha ng isang box ng $U$\n"
"ay nakikita ang mga error nito sa ibang punto sa circuit. Samakatuwid, bahagya lang ang pagtutugma ng mga bound nila, at\n"
"ang mga bound para sa mga box ng $U$ ay kailangang kalkulahin para sa mga box na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing other custom bounds {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"
msgstr "Pagsulat ng iba pang custom na bound {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same three substitutions cover other cases:\n"
msgstr "Sakop ng parehong tatlong pagpapalit ang iba pang kaso:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm.** `time_evolved_norm_forward` accepts `comm_norm_order`; passing anything\n"
"other than `2` skips the eigensolver and computes that norm directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ibang norm.** Tumatanggap ang `time_evolved_norm_forward` ng `comm_norm_order`; ang pagpasa ng anumang\n"
"bukod sa `2` ay nilalaktawan ang eigensolver at direktang kinakalkula ang norm na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different light cone.** `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` seeds a light cone from any Pauli,\n"
"and the `LightCone` constructor takes the qubits to track and the operations seeding it, so a\n"
"bound can be computed against any operator you can express that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ibang light cone.** Ang `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` ay nagtatakda ng light cone mula sa anumang Pauli,\n"
"at ang constructor ng `LightCone` ay tumatanggap ng mga qubit na susubaybayan at ang mga operasyong nagtatakda rito, kaya\n"
"maaaring kalkulahin ang bound laban sa anumang operator na maipapahayag mo sa ganitong paraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm function entirely.** `compute_bounds` only requires a callable: taking a\n"
"`Pauli` and `RotationGates` and returning a `CommutatorBounds`. Anything satisfying that signature\n"
"works, including a closed-form bound specific to your circuit family.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Isang ganap na ibang norm function.** Ang `compute_bounds` ay nangangailangan lang ng callable: na tumatanggap ng\n"
"`Pauli` at `RotationGates` at nagbabalik ng `CommutatorBounds`. Anumang tumutupad sa signature na iyon\n"
"ay gumagana, kasama ang closed-form na bound na partikular sa pamilya ng circuit mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whatever you substitute, you must prove that the result is a genuine upper bound.\n"
"Understating an error term's effect does not produce a visible failure. It produces an expectation\n"
"value that is quietly wrong, because the term will have been dropped from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anuman ang ipalit mo, kailangan mong patunayan na ang resulta ay tunay na upper bound.\n"
"Ang pagmamaliit sa epekto ng isang error term ay hindi nagdudulot ng nakikitang pagkabigo. Nagbubunga ito ng expectation\n"
"value na tahimik na mali, dahil ang term ay maaalis sa mitigated na noise model.\n"
